                    <!-- Introduction -->
                    <h2>What is this?</h2>
                    <p>
                        This website is Sorting Algorithm Visualization.
                        <br>
                        First, what is a sorting algorithm?
                        <br>
                        Imagine we have a list of numbers like [5, 4, 3, 2, 1], 
                        and that we wanted to sort them from lowest to highest.
                        <br>
                        How would you do that? You could look for the smallest one, 
                        or you might go through the list while moving each number down the list if needed.
                        <br>
                        Algorithms are step-by-step processes we take to solve a problem. 
                        Algorithms that sort things are called Sorting Algorithms.
                        <br>
                        <br>
                        Sorting Algorithms are widely used. 
                        Say that you want to look at a list of countries by alphabetization. 
                        <br>
                        We would need a Sorting Algorithm to know how to get the countries in the right order.
                        <br>
                        <br>
                        And what is a Visualization? 
                        <br>
                        Normally we cannot see a Sorting Algorithm in action, i.e. as it is changing the data.
                        <br>
                        Visualizers show the data in a way that is easy to digest, such as a graph for numbers.
                        <br>
                        <br>
                        Below, you will find some information about types of Sorting Algorithms,
                        and some basic information about specific ones.
                        <br>
                        You can click on the names of these algorithms to navigate to the visualizer screen.
                        You can also open the sidebar by pressing the button in the top left corner and click on the links there.

                    </p>
                    
